<title>UK: Tesco half year pretax profit up 10.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Tesco half year pretax profit up 10.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending August 10</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)(adjusted)  10.0		   vs 9.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.25		   vs 3.05</p>
<p> Pretax		     321		    vs 290</p>
<p> Turnover (inc VAT)     6,715		  vs 5,891</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 310 to 337 million stg.</p>
<p>Supermarket group Tesco Plc said pretax profits included an exceptional gain of five million stg on disposal of fixed assets.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 335.0		  vs 313.0</p>
<p> Interest		   14.0		   vs 23.0</p>
<p> Tax			  100.0		  vs 82.0</p>
<p> Net taxed		  226.0		  vs 208.0</p>
<p> Retained profit	  156.0		  vs 144.0</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 2</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 1</p>
<p>NOTE - Tesco Plc is Britain's leading supermarket by market share.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
